so there's been a lot of discussion of  if and when joe biden is going to  denounce  violence that is taking place in  different places around the country  and the trumpists and donald trump  himself have focused in a lot on this  why won't joe biden denounce this why  won't joe biden denounce that  now before we get to the sort of  substance  here which is that joe biden did it and  a lot of people on the left are furious  with him  and the right is just simply ignoring it  does joe biden really need to denounce  anything  in the sense that we currently have  violence happening  under the leadership of donald trump and  even though donald trump is trying to  insist that  violence is what's in store in biden's  america  if you look back at when biden was vice  president things were relatively calm  and the violence that we are seeing now  to the extent that it exists  is a a lot of it is being done by trump  supporters of course not all of it but  it is all happening  as donald trump is president of the  united states but okay  let's put that we'll table that argument  for now  and let's just say people want biden to  denounce  the violence well he did it joe biden  did it in a speech  in pennsylvania and trumpists are just  pretending that he didn't do it and some  of the left is furious so what i want to  discuss with you after we look at the  clip is  did this make sense uh let's take a look  at what joe biden had  to say rioting is not protesting  looting is not protesting setting fires  is not protesting none of this is  protesting  it's lawlessness plain and simple  and those who do it should be prosecuted  violence will not bring change it will  only bring destruction  it's wrong in every way it divides  instead of unites  destroys businesses only hurts the  working families that serve the  community  it makes things worse across the board  not better  no it's not what uh dr king or john  lewis taught  and it must end so on the facts  i agree with joe biden here rioting is  not protesting looting is not protesting  and setting fires is not protesting in  the sense that it will bring productive  change now i know that there are people  who will respond and say  you don't get to set the terms of what  counts as protesting okay well we'll get  to that in a little bit  but the possible folly of joe biden  doing this is that  the right is just pretending he didn't  do it they're continuing to say why  won't joe biden  denounce violence even though he's done  it and there's a slice of the left that  is absolutely furious with joe biden  here now i'm not saying it's all the  left or a huge portion but  it's certainly a very loud slice of the  left particularly  online and the reason that some on the  left are mad at joe biden for doing this  is  they say that he's playing into the idea  that it's his supporters who are being  violent the the idea being  by joe biden coming out and saying no  matter who's doing it i'm against the  violence  it sort of frames it up as joe biden  acknowledging that it is his supporters  being violent and telling them to stop  uh i think that there are two sides to  this so first of all  i find it completely reasonable and  unproblematic that joe biden says  violence is bad and i'm against it  it's insane that it has to be said  but he said it and he said no matter who  does the violence i'm against the  violence  but the second piece is that it's  important to clarify at every  opportunity  that almost nobody on the left is being  violent that a lot of the violence  is provocateurs and right wingers and i  hate to say this but  by and large the leftists that are being  violent  are overwhelmingly not people supporting  joe biden  and often individuals who see joe biden  as as much of a problem  or almost as much of a problem as donald  trump  so if there is a criticism of joe biden  here  it's that he arguably  indirectly or implicitly seems to be  acknowledging or conceding that some of  his supporters are being violent and i  really don't think that that's the case  at all i've not  really seen evidence of that so i don't  believe there's any problem with joe  biden  denouncing violence in principle i do  think it's sort of like when  you know there's an islamic terror  attack and right winger starts saying  why didn't this individual muslim person  who had nothing to do with it denounce  the violence well  most people denounce violence implicitly  most people are against violence i don't  know whether that  uh is even something that should be  expected particularly when joe biden  isn't in power and there's no evidence  that it is his supporters that are doing  anything but  what i would like to see more of is joe  biden aggressively placing the blame  where it should be placed biden  should be saying or let me go back there  are people saying  by doing this joe biden is hinting that  he's going to police and limit protests  as president  and limit free speech that's not at all  what biden is doing here and in fact  the obama biden administration had a  completely normal relationship with the  press  trump is the one that's authoritarian  and dystopian  when it comes to a free press and  ultimately this is a  sort of discussion of the martin luther  king perspective  on protests versus the malcolm x  perspective  and one of the things that most  resonates with me that dr king  often said was the problem  with going to looting arson violence  as a form of protest is not whether it's  morally defensible  maybe it is that's a perfectly  reasonable conversation to have  but the small percentage who choose to  do it  often end up hurting themselves and when  protests  go to violence looting etc  it very often backfires and hurts the  very people that we are trying to help  through our activism that was this is  martin luther king's view  and you can extensively find interviews  with him on youtube where he says that  that's my take on it so on the facts i  do tend to agree with joe biden  i think the framing of biden must  announce biden must denounce he does and  they just  keep saying biden must denounce as if he  didn't do it  that's where it starts to get a little  problematic
 

